        {
          "id": 1366621519,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Thanks for pointing that out. I didn't think about possible changes in the keylog file while capturing. I reverted this removal. However, having `ssh_keylog_read_file()` here may introduce inconsistencies with the hash table as the hash table is never emptied (via `g_hash_table_remove_all`) nor destroyed (via `g_hash_table_destroy`) before reopening the keylog file. Therefore, entries which were present in the keylog file during a previous call will remain stored in the hash table until the capture file is closed (and `ssh_cleanup()` is being called). If we think about the change in keylog as a simple appending another key this doesn't cause any problems. If the file can be replaced entirely, one may want to clear the hash table before reopening the keylog file.",
          "author": {
            "id": 14343997,
            "username": "Skrillor",
            "public_email": "fabian.baeumer@ruhr-uni-bochum.de",
            "name": "Fabian Bäumer",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/14343997/avatar.png?v=1776801968",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/Skrillor"
          },
